  "notes": "West leads the ♦9 against 6♠. The opening diamond lead should be won with the ♦A so that South can lead a trump towards the dummy. When West follows low, the ♠9 should be played as a safety play against West having 4 trumps to the ♠Q and ♠J.\n\nEast wins and returns a trump. West discards and dummy's ♠K wins. South still might be able to pull off a trump coup against East's remaining spade holding.\n\nSouth must reduce his trumps to the same length as East's by ruffing 2 of dummy's cards in the closed hand. The best sequence is to cash the ♥A and ♥K and play a third heart, ruffing in the closed hand.\n\nDummy can be entered in diamonds and the last heart can be ruffed. After playing a club to dummy, South can play diamonds, discarding his clubs. The trump coup will function even if East began with a singleton club.",
